    "body": "Oops, I thought I had responded earlier. We could do both!\r\n\r\nLet's say binary is installed, people can either add it themselves or do `starship launch` to launch with autopilot, we detect what shell is being used and the user and automatically do it, and switch straight into starship. :blush: \r\n\r\nMaybe even add a quick, cute ASCII animation that shows what's happening.\r\n3... 2... 1... :cloud::rocket:  \r\n\r\n### Proposed Steps\r\n1. Do `brew install starship` or `apt install starship`.\r\n2. Do `starship launch`.\r\n3. :comet: \r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
