    "created_at": "2019-05-25T16:17:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-05-25T16:24:59Z",
    "body": "After a good amount of testing in [basic-init branch](https://github.com/starship/starship/tree/basic-init), it looks like we can't get enough context from environment variables alone to identify the shell. Fish is able to be reliably identified with `$SHELL`, but it appears zsh and bash don't export the environment variables that would make them identifiable (`$BASH` or `$SHELL`).\r\n\r\nThough it's a little more inelegant, my next thought is to do the following:\r\n```bash\r\neval $(SHELL=zsh starship init)\r\n\r\n# or \r\n\r\nexport STARSHIP_SHELL=zsh\r\neval $(starship init)\r\n```\r\n\r\nDoes anyone have other ideas? 🤔 ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
